<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Present or absent predictions for 12432 species-structure pairs across 48 held-out bird species, made from Uberon taxon constraints alone, with no bird trait data read." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "For each of the 48 species on the frozen Aves roster and each of the 259 Uberon core terms that carry a taxon constraint, the tool predicted present or absent and said on what basis. A structure is predicted absent when Uberon's never_in_taxon covers the species, or when in_taxon names a clade the species is outside. It is predicted present with a stated basis when in_taxon or present_in_taxon names a clade below Vertebrata containing the species, and present by default otherwise. Because the predictions come only from taxon constraints, they are identical for species inside the same constrained clade: across the roster there are 2 distinct prediction vectors. The builder stayed blind to the clade throughout: the blueprint tool refuses descriptions that resolve inside it, and the leak check over this folder exits 0." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "blind prediction set from ontology constraints" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Made before any scoring, against an exam frozen and checksummed by another thread, from identifiers in that exam file and the ontologies only. No bird trait table, genome, occurrence count or atlas was opened. The predictions file cites the exam's SHA-256 so the order of events can be checked." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-aves-exam-and-predictions> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Score the predictions against a trait source for the roster, structure by structure, counting accuracy separately for the stated and the default rows. The informative case is a structure that varies within the held-out clade: taxon constraints cannot distinguish species that the ontology does not distinguish, so a prediction set like this one must fail on exactly those structures." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Does not establish: that any bird has or lacks a structure. A \"present by default\" row says only that the ontology does not exclude the structure, which is not evidence of presence, and the set cannot distinguish species that Uberon treats alike. Accuracy on this set would measure Uberon's taxon constraints, not an organism model." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-aves-blind-predictions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/main/organism-design/exam/aves-predictions.json> .
}
